From d609de89cf36427b176e2223796bdf8363318f10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lemonade1921 <joandegenover1@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:33:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Smooth trackpad pinch-to-zoom on macOS

On macOS a trackpad pinch arrives as a burst of ctrl+wheel events with small
fractional deltas. Each event was mapped to a full zoomIn()/zoomOut() step and
a full re-render, so pinching jumped through zoom levels and stuttered.

Add Common.Utils.SmoothWheelZoom: while the fingers move, the already drawn
document canvases are scaled with a CSS transform (GPU only, every frame,
e^(-deltaY/100) like Chromium's pinch scale). When the gesture pauses the real
zoom is applied once, and the preview transform is dropped in the same task the
editor repaints its main canvas, so there's no flash or jump. Used by the
document, spreadsheet, presentation, PDF and diagram editors for pixel-precise
wheel input on macOS; line/page-mode mouse wheels keep the stepped zoom.
